# DigitalOcean Spaces test behavior

- `lib/testUtilities/setup.ts` already mocks `lib/storage/storageAPI` globally.
- Do not add another `jest.mock` or module replacement for `storageAPI` in an
  individual test. A second mock can replace the shared in-memory behavior.
- Exercise storage wrappers through their normal APIs. Verify writes by reading
  the object back and comparing its bytes; verify cleanup by confirming the
  object is no longer readable.
- When a failure path must be simulated, configure the existing global mock
  function rather than replacing the `storageAPI` module:

```ts
jest.mocked(putObject).mockRejectedValue(new Error('storage unavailable'));
```

- Tests must never make real DigitalOcean Spaces/S3 reads or writes.
